descriptionByLocale.en:
Public competition at the City of Mendrisio.

Location: Installer or 100% electric installer.

Dicastery Institutions and resources Administrative Section Cancelleria Via Municipio 13 6850 Mendrisio 058 688 31 10 stationary@mendrisio.ch Res. mun. 5773 of 15.09.2026 18 September 2026 Competition for the recruitment of a Installer or a 100% electric installer, at an indefinite time, at the Municipal Company (AIMsio) of the City of Drinking Required conditions: The owner of the function, included in the Drinking Water Section of AIM, AP Plant and Quality Office, will have the following main tasks:
• to collaborate in the phase of study, realization and commissioning of new aqueduct plants;
• co-ordinate the ordinary maintenance of drinking plants and aqueduct infrastructure in accordance with the provisions of self-control provided by Swiss food legislation;
• operate as a reference person for fault management, ordinary maintenance and improvement interventions regarding telemanagement and electrical installations;
• keep the documentation inherent to the plants per day;
• provide availability to participate in the regular picket service. In addition:
• other work assignments compatible with its function and its competences may be or are given to it;
• can be called or called to provide service at irregular times, even out of time and on public holidays according to the needs of service. City of Mendrisio Competition 2/3 Requirements:
• Federal Certificate of Capacity (AFC) as Electrical Installer;
• experience in aqueducts can be preferential title;
• good knowledge of MS Windows operating system and its MS Office tools;
• good relational, organizational, communication and analytical skills;
• license to conduct category B;
• Swiss citizenship or home in Switzerland. Preferential securities may be set up:
• availability to obtain the diploma of Fontaniere/a AFP;
• knowledge of a second national language (German or French). Gross annual wage (threeteenth monthly and salary scale updated at 01.01.2026): - Classes (4)* 5 - 7 ROD (Operation/or craftsman function); - Minimum: CHF 62’022.-- yearly; (*CHF 58’371.-- yearly) - Maximum: CHF 85’327.-- yearly; - In addition to the salary is paid, to the entitled, the allowance for children according to LAFam. * In the event of intake of employees with little experience or for which it is reasonably necessary to foresee an introduction period, the Town Hall can establish a lower initial salary of a class than the minimum entry class. Within the framework of the above-mentioned possibilities of pay, the City Hall can recognize the activity carried out previously, if conformed to this Chapter, assigning one or more year of service pursuant to art. 29 cpv. 2 ROD. Working week: 40 hours Degree of employment: 100% Start of activity: As soon as possible. Deadline for competition: Applications must be submitted via the application form by Friday 9 October 2026 at 23:59, accompanied by the following documents: - presentation letter; - curriculum vitae with photos; - copies of certificates of study and work; - self-certification on good conduct and any executive procedures; - questionnaire on health. Applications submitted in another form will not be considered. City of Mendrisio Competition 3/3 This notice of competition and its application form are also available on the https://www.mendrisio.ch/concourses. The Human Resources Section remains at the courteous disposal (tel. +41 58 688 33 10) of those who do not have a device (PC, tablet, smartphone, scanner, etc.) to provide them with the necessary tools to send their application through the prescribed application form. In addition to the documents to be attached to the application, at a later time may be required to present the extract of the court for private individuals and the extract of the execution register (validity 6 months). The City Hall reserves the right to change the tasks at any time, in relation to any changes in the regulations and regulations in force. It is the faculty of the City Hall to proceed with a pre-selection of candidates and candidates for the call to hearings. The City Hall reserves the right not to proceed with recruitment, in the absence of candidates or candidates eligible for the function. Legal remedies Against the notice of competition shall be the right to appeal to the Lodging Council of State within 30 days of the date of publication. Detailed information can be obtained from the Directorate AIM, Via Municipio 13, Mendrisio, tel. 058 688 38 00. The Town Hall

Registration deadline: 2026-10-09.

